# tools/radial_paint_witness.rish -- a RADIAL positioned gradient SEEN on a real image proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the sibling of tools/gradient_paint_witness.rish, which proved the LINEAR gradient
# family (horizontal, vertical, and the diagonal pair). This rung proves the RADIAL shape: a pixel's ramp position is its
# distance from the box center, so the center is the first control exactly and every corner the last, each ring between one
# constant color (the CSS radial-gradient shape). Stands on the positioned ramp (image/color_ramp_stops.rye), the open
# color algebra (image/color.rye), and the open QOI codec (image/qoi.rye).
# Design read: active-designing/20260816-210735_season-g-color-algebra-crux.md (the color floor this stands on).
# Teacher, thanked clean-room: gratitude/w3c-css-color.md (the W3C CSS Color / Images specs -- public standards only).
#
# The crux this witness proves is that a radial positioned gradient becomes a real image: paint_gradient_radial fills a box
# where each pixel is the color the positioned ramp samples at its distance from the center. The center pixel is the first
# control exactly and every corner the last, byte-for-byte; the four edge midpoints share one constant ring color (a true
# circle); the position grows with the radius; uneven positions bend the disc where even spacing cannot; the disc
# round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte; a sub-rectangle paints only its own box (the ground stays); a
# non-square box still centers and corners exactly; a single-pixel box, a zero dimension, an out-of-bounds box, and a
# non-ascending ramp refuse by name having painted nothing. Compose not braid -- color_ramp_stops decides the color, qoi
# owns the target, color composites; this rung only routes each pixel to its radial position. The routing is integer
# fixed-point (an integer square root, no float) so a disc is deterministic. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/radial_paint_witness.rish

say "radial-paint: Language EN -- Season G's radial positioned gradient painted onto an image; a keeper names a stop list and reads back a gradient disc a surface can show, on our own color model and open codec."
say "radial-paint: Style Radiant -- compose not braid; color_ramp_stops DECIDES each pixel's color, qoi owns the RGBA target, color composites src-over, and this rung only ROUTES each pixel to its distance from the center so a translucent disc tints the picture beneath."
say "radial-paint: Lens TAME -- the whole box bound-checked ONCE up front in u64 so a far edge can never wrap; the ramp validated ONCE before any pixel so a malformed disc refuses having painted nothing; the radius routed through an integer square root (no float) so a disc is deterministic; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/radial_paint"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/radial_paint.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "radial-paint: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "radial-paint: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "radial-paint: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-radial-paint" else "radial-paint: selftest did not print the GREEN radial-paint line"

assert selftest.out contains "round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte" else "radial-paint: the painted disc did not prove its QOI round trip"

assert selftest.out contains "share one constant ring color" else "radial-paint: the disc did not prove its rings are constant (radial symmetry)"

assert selftest.out contains "the position grows with the radius" else "radial-paint: the disc did not prove its position grows with the radius"

assert selftest.out contains "bend the disc where even spacing cannot" else "radial-paint: the disc did not prove it bends with position"

say "radial-paint: GREEN -- a radial positioned gradient painted onto a real image, its center and corners exact, its rings constant, its radius monotonic, its bend measured, its round trip byte-for-byte, proven on metal."
